  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for libXi",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for libXi fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93541: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XQueryDeviceState() (bsc#1281605).\n- CVE-2026-93542: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XI2 class parsing via size_classes() and copy_classes() (bsc#1281606).\n- CVE-2026-93543: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XI2 class parser (bsc#1281608).\n- CVE-2026-93544: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XI2 XIQueryDevice reply parsing (bsc#1281609).\n- CVE-2026-93545: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XListInputDevices() (bsc#1281612).\n- CVE-2026-94281: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XListInputDevices() class parsing (bsc#1281615).\n- CVE-2026-94282: Out-of-bounds read in libXi's XI2 enter/leave/focus cookie conversion (bsc#1281651).\n- CVE-2026-109089: XGetDeviceControl Control Type Mismatch Heap Buffer Overflow (bsc#1285084).\n- CVE-2026-109090: XGetDeviceControl DEVICE_ENABLE Heap Buffer Overflow (bsc#1285085).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
